## Chapter 1.1: Bella Thorne - The Architect of Friendship {#chapter-1.1-bella-thorne---the-architect-of-friendship-1 .unnumbered}

> The synthetic thud of her riﬂe stock hitting the composite ﬂoor echoed
> ﬂatly in the gymnasium\'s vast, cavernous space. Bella Thorne, barely
> an adult, moved through the practiced motions of the Close Quarters
> Battle drill with a precision that bordered on the preternatural. Her
> uniform, stiﬀ and unyielding, chafed subtly under the arms, but she
> barely registered it. *Slam. Click. Step. Scan. Repeat.* The movements
> were ingrained, muscle memory perfected years ago, leaving her mind
> free to wander, to escape the crushing monotony of it all.
>
> The gymnasium itself was a monument to functional drabness:
